# <%= current_page.data.title %>

You'll find runbooks here on managing resource or access requests, like environments with GPU access or an increase to Justice AI Gateway allowances.

## Increase AI usage limits for a project

The approved increase should be applied by an AI Gateway administrator with the required permissions:

1. Identify the project ID in/from the request from the user.
1. Log in to https://admin.ai-gateway.justice.gov.uk/.
1. Navigate to Teams.
1. Select the Team ID corresponding to the project ID.
1. Go to Settings > Edit Settings.
1. Update Max Budget (USD) to the approved value.
1. Save the change.
1. Confirm the outcome with the requester in the original Slack thread.

## Give a user or team access to ingestion

This service was originally created to enable `sftp` file transfer to the `analytical-platform-data-production` AWS Account.
It can now also be used to ingest files to a non-`analytical-platform-data-production` MoJ AWS Account, and for users to collect files from `analytical-platform-data-production` after they have been ingested there for enrichment purposes (`user-with-egress`).

### Pre-requisites

- Users must supply the information specified in the user guidance.
- Read the guidance on [working with Terraform modules on the Modernisation Platform](../routine-maintenance/analytical-platform/operational-runbooks/working-with-terraform-mod-platform) if you're not familiar with working in Modernisation Platform environments.

There are two types of user that can be added to ingestion:

* [`user`](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform-environments/tree/main/terraform/environments/analytical-platform-ingestion/modules/transfer-family/user): with target location either in `analytical-platform-data-production` or in another MoJ AWS Account
* [`user-with-egress`](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform-environments/tree/main/terraform/environments/analytical-platform-ingestion/modules/transfer-family/user-with-egress): in which the user ingests data into `analytical-platform-data-production`, whereupon it is enriched, and then collected by the user

### Adding a `user`

1. Open the [modernisation-platform-environments repository](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform-environments/).

2. Add a new entry to either production or development, in the `environment-configuration.tf` file under the `transfer_server_sftp_users` section specifying the `username`, `ssh_key` and `cidr_block`.
(The CIDR block is created from the given IP address using suffix `/32` indicating a single address).

3. If the target location is **not in `analytical-platform-data-production`** then it must be added to the `target_buckets` list; if it is KMS encrypted add the KMS key to the `target_kms_keys` list.
(For `analytical-platform-data-production` buckets this step is taken care of automatically).
If the user has specified a prefix (eg `<bucketname>/<prefix>`) do not include the prefix in the `target_buckets` list, it can be included when populating the target bucket secret, see step 6b below.

4. Commit your changes; push your changes to a branch and create a PR in which you should

   a. Outline the intent of the PR.

   b. Link the issue / task in the PR description.

5. Apply to the appropriate environment:

   a. `development` - navigate to [Actions](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform-environments/actions) in the repository, select the `analytical-platform-ingestion` workflow and apply it.

   b. `production` - these can only be made when the PR is approved and merged. Navigate to [Actions](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform-environments/actions), select the `analytical-platform-ingestion` workflow and apply it on `main`.

6. As part of the onboarding process, users must supply an email and target location. We use these to manually populate the secrets generated by terraform when the above process is complete.

   To populate a new secret:

   > Navigate to AWS Secrets Manager > Secrets > `<Secret>` > Retrieve Secret Value > Set Secret Value > Select Plaintext and overwrite `{}` with the required value.

   a. **Email:** Populate the secret `ingestion/sftp/<user>/technical-contact` with the email address.

   b. **Target Bucket:** Populate the secret `ingestion/sftp/<user>/target-bucket` with the specified target bucket, supplied by the user. If the user has specified a bucket prefix it can be added here `<bucketname>/<prefix>` (no leading S3 needed).
   NB: If the user does not specify a prefix then the `username` is automatically added as a prefix:

   i. secret value = `<bucketname>` -> destination = `<bucketname>/<username>`

   ii. secret value = `<bucketname>/<prefix>` -> destination = `<bucketname>/<prefix>`

> The destination bucket *must* have the correct permissions applied to allow the `transfer` Lambda to transfer files to it.
>
> The user requesting access to ingestion is responsible for ensuring that the destination S3 bucket allows ingestion to write to it. If the bucket uses a customer-managed KMS key, the user must also apply the required permissions to the KMS key.
>
> See the [user guidance](https://user-guidance.analytical-platform.service.justice.gov.uk/tools/ingestion/#user-action-required) for the permissions that need to be applied.

### Adding a `user-with-egress`

1. Open the [modernisation-platform-environments repository](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform-environments/).

2. Add a new entry to either production or development, in the `environment-configuration.tf` file, in the `transfer_server_sftp_users_with_egress` section specifying the `username`, `ssh_key` and `cidr_block`, `egress_bucket` and `egress_bucket_kms_key`

3. Commit your changes.

4. Push your changes to a branch.

5. Create a PR.

   a. Outline the intent of the PR.

   b. Link the issue / task in the PR description.

6. Apply to the appropriate environment:

   a. `development` - navigate to [Actions](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform-environments/actions) in the repository, select the `analytical-platform-ingestion` workflow and apply it.

   b. `production` - these can only be made when the PR is approved and merged. Navigate to [Actions](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform-environments/actions), select the `analytical-platform-ingestion` workflow and apply it on `main`.

7. As part of the onboarding process, users must supply an email and target location. We use these to manually populate the secrets generated by terraform when the above process is complete.

   To populate a new secret:

   > Navigate to AWS Secrets Manager > Secrets > `<Secret>` > Retrieve Secret Value > Set Secret Value > Select Plaintext and overwrite `{}` with the required value.

   a. **Email:** Populate the secret `ingestion/sftp/<user>/technical-contact` with the email address.

   b. **Target Bucket:** Populate the secret `ingestion/sftp/<user>/target-bucket` with the specified target bucket, supplied by the user.
